{"name":"Biloxi","hex":"#f4e4cd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Biloxi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A member of a Native American people formerly inhabiting an area near the coast of the Gulf of Mexico in southeast Mississippi."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The extinct Siouan language once spoken by the Biloxi.","A city in and one of the two county seats of Harrison County, Mississippi, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Biloxi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biloxi, Mississippi","blocks":[{"text":"Biloxi is a city in Harrison County, Mississippi, United States. It lies on the Gulf Coast in southern Mississippi, bordering the city of Gulfport to its west. The adjacent cities are both designated as seats of Harrison County. The population of Biloxi was 49,449 at the 2020 census, making it the state's fourth-most populous city. It is a principal city of the Gulfport–Biloxi metropolitan area, home to 416,259 residents in 2020. The area's first European settlers were French colonists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BiloxiLightHouseandVisitorsCenter.jpg/330px-BiloxiLightHouseandVisitorsCenter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biloxi%2C_Mississippi"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/WC-130J_taking_off_from_Keesler_Air_Force_Base_in_Mississippi.jpg/500px-WC-130J_taking_off_from_Keesler_Air_Force_Base_in_Mississippi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/WC-130J_taking_off_from_Keesler_Air_Force_Base_in_Mississippi.jpg/1280px-WC-130J_taking_off_from_Keesler_Air_Force_Base_in_Mississippi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/WC-130J_taking_off_fr